@@ -128,3 +129,99 @@ audited administrative resolution exists.
 This policy is tested with Node22, isolated local Mongo and synthetic external
 providers. Actual Atlas tier, production Mongo/topology, orchestrator, provider
 access, immutable images, rollback and full-stack release gates remain open.
+
+## Reviewed signing and read-only recovery (LT-140 / LT-127)
+
+Writes require the approved LT-1 r2 contract at Bridge commit
+`a67d9d8b7efd9189f76885ecbd6394a9f3d92f54` plus the Chief's expiry, evidence
+and readiness addendum. Required signing does not widen the Johnny sandbox,
+replace project edit permission, expose Bridge or provision production keys.
+
+The authenticated matrix and queue share the same flow:
+
+1. Preview/restore-preview/revise returns authoritative `review_binding`, exact
+   before/after HTML and integer Unix `review_expires_at`. Conductor validates the
+   binding shape, stored page identity and full HTML hashes, then stores it with
+   an opaque local review ID, verified actor, hashed local session association,
+   selected inputs, section identity and evidence revision. The browser cannot
+   replace the binding or supply a signer identity.
+2. Explicit confirmation sends the local review ID and compatibility token/hash.
+   Conductor rechecks current permission, session, section, inputs and expiry.
+   Node 22 native Ed25519 signs the stored binding; no `EdDSA` fallback is used.
+3. A single Mongo Project update consumes that review, sets the section's pending
+   claim, and appends the issuer/jti intent **before** external dispatch. A failed
+   claim prevents dispatch. Intents and response events append to Project-level
+   `remedyOperations`, excluded from ordinary reads and retained across TOC section
+   replacement. Assertions and private keys are never stored there.
+4. Conductor sends one mutation to the explicitly configured authenticated engine;
+   redirects and mutation retries are disabled. Its assertion expires at the
+   minimum of `iat+60`, authoritative review expiry and local key-not-after.
+   Expired or too-short reviews require a new preview and confirmation.
+
+The signer additionally requires these deployment settings (names only):
+
+| Setting | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `REMEDY_REVIEWER_SIGNING_KEY_FILE` | File-backed Ed25519 private PEM; mount privately for the Conductor runtime only |
+| `REMEDY_REVIEWER_KEY_ID` | Exact key ID provisioned in Bridge's approved keyring |
+| `REMEDY_REVIEWER_ISSUER` / `REMEDY_REVIEWER_AUDIENCE` | Exact environment-specific values accepted by that Bridge deployment |
+| `REMEDY_REVIEWER_KEY_ENABLED` | Exact `true` to admit signing; default unavailable |
+| `REMEDY_REVIEWER_KEY_NOT_BEFORE` / `REMEDY_REVIEWER_KEY_NOT_AFTER` | Explicit integer Unix-second validity window aligned with Bridge's key policy |
+
+Signer misconfiguration blocks mutation admission without crashing ordinary
+Conductor startup or preventing an otherwise configured scan route. Effective
+health capability reports mutation unavailable when signing is unavailable. The
+public deterministic LT-1 fixture key is rejected for production even if renamed.
+This implementation supplies no real key, mount, rotation or live rollout.
+Disable signing before emergency revocation; coordinate a new key ID and Bridge
+keyring policy through the approved operator process. Do not log key values or
+compact assertions or put them into frontend configuration.
+
+Pending claims freeze certification while retaining the underlying old scan for
+possible **confirmed matched-source no-op** preservation. Only exact durable
+outcome metadata can complete the direct-response claim: `no_change` preserves
+current evidence; proven `stale_preview`/`target_mismatch` invalidates old evidence
+even for `not_attempted`; known writes invalidate and request a new scan. A matched
+no-op does not need a rescan to preserve evidence when the scanner is unavailable.
+Unknown/malformed/transport-loss or pending results keep the page blocked;
+unknown mutation invalidates evidence. A generic HTTP 4xx or `applied:false`
+without the approved metadata never releases the claim or proves a no-op.
+
+An authorized original reviewer (or existing support/superadmin) can explicitly
+read `GET …/workqueue/page/:sectionID/operations/:localOperationID`. Conductor
+rechecks current project edit access and the saved project/section/actor mapping,
+then sends only the stored issuer/jti to authenticated engine operation-status.
+It returns whitelisted durable outcome metadata, not HTML, assertions, bindings,
+key details or arbitrary upstream errors. A browser-supplied issuer/jti/remote
+operation ID cannot select another operation. A 404 is not proof that no write
+occurred. Polling never resubmits a mutation, updates operation history, repairs
+an audit, releases a claim or enables scanning. The UI provides an explicit
+“Read operation evidence” action after interruption and after remount.
+
+Administrative claim resolution remains a separate audited workflow. Even a
+read-only lookup that reports known success after a lost reply leaves the local
+pending claim intact. Operators must retain the original intent/outcome, Bridge
+ledger/fence/audit/snapshots and CXone state; no automatic unlock or remote retry
+is implemented. Back up Project operation history with sections, conformance
+records and work items. Reconcile it with Bridge's trust epoch before enabling
+writes after restore; never discard an unknown intent during rollback.
+
+Operation history appends inside Project and therefore shares Mongo's document
+size limit. LT-128's history growth/read bounds and production storage assessment
+remain release gates; no pruning or retention policy is introduced. Component
+route/mounted-form and frozen positive-vector tests do not prove the final
+Conductor → actual Server → actual Bridge flow, durable Bridge crash/fence/replay
+behavior, Linux/container topology or production key provisioning. Those remain
+mandatory coordinated release gates. No signed-flow TestSprite plan was created.
+
+A validated preview can itself prove that the page changed before preview. Before
+storing its local review, Conductor compares the authoritative full source digest
+with supported stored scan hashes (Bridge's 16-character SHA256 prefix or a full
+64-character digest). Different or unknown existing evidence hashes atomically
+invalidate source/rendered evidence and advance the review's evidence revision;
+absent evidence remains absent. A later `no_change` result for the new source
+cannot revive the old review. `evidenceChanged` refreshes the mounted matrix and
+reviewer forms without another external scan or mutation. TOC merges likewise
+clear source/rendered evidence and current preview when URL or numeric page ID
+changes, preserving section identity, manual checkboxes and other history. A
+title-only refresh on the same target preserves current evidence and preview.
